{"slug":"marsha-blackburn","qid":"Q458971","name":"Marsha Blackburn","desc":"American businesswoman and politician (born 1952)","article":"Marsha Blackburn","born":"1952-06-06","died":null,"birthplace":"Laurel","parties":["Republican Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Senator","w":"Tennessee","f":2019,"u":null},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"TN-07","f":2003,"u":2019},{"t":"State Senate of Tennessee","w":"","f":1999,"u":2003}],"summary":"Mary Marsha Blackburn (née Wedgeworth; born June 6, 1952) is an American politician and businesswoman who is the governor-elect of Tennessee and the state's senior United States senator, a seat she has held since 2019. A member of the Republican Party, Blackburn was a state senator from 1999 to 2003 and represented Tennessee's 7th congressional district in the United States House of Representatives from 2003 to 2019, during which time the National Journal rated her among the House's most conservative members.\nA supporter of the Tea Party movement, Blackburn is a staunch ally of President Donald Trump.","photo":{"f":"marsha-blackburn.jpg","by":"United States Senate Photographic Studio","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sen._Marsha_Blackburn_(R-TN)_official_headshot_-_116th_Congress.jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"G","k":"TN-GOV","p":"R","n":"Marsha Blackburn","race":"TN-GOV"},{"y":2024,"o":"S","k":"TN","p":"R","v":1918743,"s":63.8,"w":true,"n":"Marsha Blackburn"},{"y":2018,"o":"S","k":"TN","p":"R","v":1227483,"s":54.71,"w":true,"n":"Marsha Blackburn"},{"y":2016,"o":"H","k":"TN-07","p":"R","v":200407,"s":72.22,"w":true,"n":"Marsha Blackburn"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"TN-07","p":"R","v":110534,"s":70.0,"w":true,"n":"Marsha Blackburn"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"TN-07","p":"R","v":182730,"s":71.02,"w":true,"n":"Marsha Blackburn"},{"y":2010,"o":"H","k":"TN-07","p":"R","v":158916,"s":72.37,"w":true,"n":"Marsha Blackburn"},{"y":2008,"o":"H","k":"TN-07","p":"R","v":217332,"s":68.58,"w":true,"n":"Marsh